---
import { Code } from 'astro:components';

const spliceSnippet = `var view pb.OpaquePeerUpdate
_ = view.Unmarshal(pkt)
router := view.GetRouterId() // skips #1
view.SetActive(false)        // marks #3 dirty
pkt = view.MarshalAppend(nil)`;

const pbStructSnippet = `pkt, _ := omnibuf.Marshal(&pb.Node{Id: 1, City: "FRA"})`;

const plainStructSnippet = `type Node struct {
  ID   uint32 \`omnibuf:"1"\`
  City string \`omnibuf:"2"\`
}
pkt, _ := omnibuf.Marshal(&Node{ID: 1, City: "FRA"})`;
---

<section id="motivation" class="py-12 sm:py-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-7xl mx-auto">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight uppercase leading-none">
      Faster, inspectable,{' '}
      <span class="font-serif italic font-normal normal-case text-[#FF4F18]">and spliceable.</span>
    </h2>
  </div>

  <div class="border-t-2 border-ink divide-y-2 divide-ink/20">
    <!-- 1. INSPECTABLE WITHOUT A SCHEMA -->
    <div
      id="inspectable-without-schema"
      class="scroll-mt-16 py-8 sm:py-10 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-6 lg:gap-8 items-center"
    >
      <div class="lg:col-span-5 space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold uppercase tracking-tight leading-snug">
          Read packets without a schema.
        </h3>
        <!-- prettier-ignore -->
        <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-ink/90 leading-relaxed max-w-[60ch]">
          Protobuf packs strings, byte slices, sub-messages, maps, and arrays into a single wire type, and mixes booleans, unsigned ints, and signed ints together. Looking at a raw packet without the <code>.proto</code> file leaves you guessing what each field is. OmniBuf puts an explicit type on every field (16 wire types in total), so any tool can decode exact values from raw bytes. Turning on optional <strong>Field #0</strong> metadata also writes the field names once at the top of the packet.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-7 min-w-0">
        <div class="os-window overflow-hidden font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <div class="os-titlebar bg-[#E5E0D5]">
            <span class="font-bold uppercase text-ink text-xs">raw packet dump</span>
            <div class="os-stripes"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-ink text-paper p-4 space-y-3">
            <div class="bg-[#1F1F1F] p-3 rounded border border-paper/15">
              <div class="text-[11px] uppercase font-bold text-[#FF4F18] mb-1.5">Protobuf</div>
              <pre class="leading-relaxed overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="text-[#FF4F18] font-bold">1:</span> 1          <span class="text-paper/55"># bool / uint / sint / enum?</span>
<span class="text-[#FF4F18] font-bold">2:</span> 3          <span class="text-paper/55"># +3 uint or -2 sint?</span>
<span class="text-[#FF4F18] font-bold">3:</span> &#123;<span class="text-acid">"FRA"</span>&#125;    <span class="text-paper/55"># string / bytes / sub-msg?</span>
<span class="text-[#FF4F18] font-bold">4:</span> <span class="text-acid">"\x0a\x14"</span> <span class="text-paper/55"># bytes / string / packed array?</span></code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-[#1F1F1F] p-3 rounded border border-acid/40">
              <div class="text-[11px] uppercase font-bold text-acid mb-1.5">OmniBuf</div>
              <pre class="leading-relaxed overflow-x-auto"><code><span class="text-acid font-bold">1:</span> <span class="text-[#FF4F18] font-bold">true</span>       <span class="text-acid/80"># bool (0 value bytes)</span>
<span class="text-acid font-bold">2:</span> -2         <span class="text-acid/80"># signed int</span>
<span class="text-acid font-bold">3:</span> <span class="text-acid">"FRA"</span>      <span class="text-acid/80"># utf8 string</span>
<span class="text-acid font-bold">4:</span> [10, 20]   <span class="text-acid/80"># 2 uints</span></code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 2. READ OR SPLICE WITHOUT DECODING -->
    <div
      id="read-or-splice"
      class="scroll-mt-16 py-8 sm:py-10 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-6 lg:gap-8 items-center"
    >
      <div class="lg:col-span-5 space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold uppercase tracking-tight leading-snug">
          Read or edit one field in place.
        </h3>
        <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-ink/90 leading-relaxed max-w-[60ch]">
          Routers and proxies often need to inspect a single header field or flip a flag inside a
          payload. Every integer and container in OmniBuf starts with its byte length, so a reader
          can jump straight over earlier fields. Generated <code>Opaque</code> views read one tag or
          splice a new value directly into the byte slice.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-7 min-w-0">
        <div class="os-window overflow-hidden font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <div class="os-titlebar bg-[#E5E0D5]">
            <span class="font-bold uppercase text-ink text-xs">splice.go</span>
            <div class="os-stripes"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-ink text-paper p-4 [&>pre]:!bg-transparent [&>pre]:!p-0 [&>pre]:!m-0 [&>pre]:!border-0 [&>pre]:leading-relaxed [&>pre]:overflow-x-auto">
            <Code code={spliceSnippet} lang="go" theme="github-dark" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 3. PROTOBUF + GRPC OR PLAIN STRUCTS -->
    <div
      id="proto-or-plain-structs"
      class="scroll-mt-16 py-8 sm:py-10 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-6 lg:gap-8 items-center"
    >
      <div class="lg:col-span-5 space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold uppercase tracking-tight leading-snug">
          Use .proto files or plain structs.
        </h3>
        <!-- prettier-ignore -->
        <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-ink/90 leading-relaxed max-w-[60ch]">
          OmniBuf is a message serialization format, not a new RPC protocol. Most <a href="https://grpc.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="doc-link">gRPC</a> and <a href="https://connectrpc.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="doc-link">Connect</a> libraries let you register a custom wire codec in a few lines of code and keep your existing <code>.proto</code> files. Or skip <code>.proto</code> files altogether: add <a href="/go#struct-tags" class="doc-link">Go struct tags</a> (<code>omnibuf:"1"</code>) or call <a href="/es#define-message" class="doc-link">TypeScript <code>defineMessage</code></a>, and both paths produce the exact same wire bytes.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-7 min-w-0">
        <div class="os-window overflow-hidden font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <div class="os-titlebar bg-[#E5E0D5]">
            <span class="font-bold uppercase text-ink text-xs">marshal.go</span>
            <div class="os-stripes"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-ink text-paper p-4 space-y-3">
            <div class="bg-[#1F1F1F] p-3 rounded border border-paper/15 [&>pre]:!bg-transparent [&>pre]:!p-0 [&>pre]:!m-0 [&>pre]:!border-0 [&>pre]:leading-relaxed [&>pre]:overflow-x-auto">
              <div class="text-[11px] uppercase font-bold text-paper/65 mb-1">From .proto</div>
              <Code code={pbStructSnippet} lang="go" theme="github-dark" />
            </div>
            <div class="bg-[#1F1F1F] p-3 rounded border border-paper/15 [&>pre]:!bg-transparent [&>pre]:!p-0 [&>pre]:!m-0 [&>pre]:!border-0 [&>pre]:leading-relaxed [&>pre]:overflow-x-auto">
              <div class="text-[11px] uppercase font-bold text-paper/65 mb-1">Struct tags</div>
              <Code code={plainStructSnippet} lang="go" theme="github-dark" />
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-3 py-2 rounded bg-acid text-ink font-bold text-xs border border-ink">
              <span class="uppercase">Wire bytes (7B)</span>
              <span>21 03 55 07 46 52 41</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
